## SELinux successor — 2026-11-08

Eight shared-label real probes passed, with concurrent Ruff/Bandit findings,
unchanged source hashes and container removal. Public Ox wrapper clean probe
exited zero. Local suite: 28 tests, one real opt-in skipped; platform: 70 tests.
E-SELINUX-LOCAL replaces changed-input contract observations; AC-01/02 retain
bounded local approval. AC-03 remains UNVERIFIED for the larger operational
matrix. Previous contract/governance/preflight records remain historical.

## Cleanup inspection successor — 2026-11-09

The maintainer redirected the cleanup request to Ox only and prohibited tests,
verification scripts, commits and publication for this task. Static inspection
removed unreachable central-scanner setup after the toolbox branch exits, and a
repeated coverage condition. Public commands, native dispatch, report validation,
rules and fixtures remain unchanged in scope. Python bytecode caches were removed
after copying their bytes and metadata; their source files remain present.

AC-01/02 are INCONCLUSIVE on these changed implementation inputs: the previous
tests and their original hashes remain preserved in evidence.json and historical
artifacts; no test result was renewed. AC-03 remains UNVERIFIED. This record does
not adjudicate later operational artifacts or claim current Docker qualification.
The manual control-flow argument, input identities, preservation observations,
recovery and remaining gaps are in
the cleanup report (`docs/validation/repository-cleanup-20261109/report.md`).

## Consumer guide alignment — 2026-11-09

REQ-01/02 -> D-25/R-25 -> T025: wrapper now leaves SELinux label unset unless
the caller selects it; updated test source expects unset. Native exec, argv,
exit forwarding and discovery remain. Scripts documentation follows the observed
consumer-integration/application guides, including explicit host relabel effects.
AC-01/02 remain INCONCLUSIVE: manual review is not a current contract test result;
AC-03 remains UNVERIFIED. Earlier evidence.json records and logs are unchanged,
not rehashed into a fresh approval. Execution restrictions from the prior request
were retained; no verifier, test, Docker probe or scanner was invoked.
See inputs, review and recovery (`docs/validation/toolbox-consumer-alignment-20261109/report.md`).

