## Mandatory consumer rules successor — 2026-11-09

REQ-01/02 -> D-26/R-26 -> T026: removed duplicate host commands for central
scanners, ineffective scanner exports and unreachable local report handling.
Plans choose the transport before command construction; unavailable local tools
have empty argv. Native scanner argv, report checks, age policy, discovery and
caller-controlled mounts are retained. Consumer documentation now accurately
describes central automatic OSV acquisition and its distinct 12h acquisition age.

Focused public CLI tests: 30 executed, 29 passed, one real-Docker opt-in skipped;
includes aliases, clean/findings, malformed/missing diagnostics, cleanup failures,
source/mode/inventory mutations, paths/argv, missing local tools and SELinux
forwarding. Static inventory: all 11 native config files referenced, no legacy
JSON/locks. These observations support T026 configuration conformity; broader
AC-01/02 remain INCONCLUSIVE because no full feature acceptance/freshness run was
performed on all current inputs. AC-03 remains UNVERIFIED: no real Docker scanner
or OSV acquisition observed here. Historical evidence.json/logs are unchanged.
Current inputs, source bytes, patches and test output:
consumer rules report (`docs/validation/toolbox-consumer-rules-20261109/report.md`).

